          %h2#notation Notation
          %p
            For the following discussion we suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi: X\to S
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+scheme"} smooth
            map of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d:\mathcal{O}_X\to \Omega^1_{X/S}
            be the standard differential. It is an integrable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connection"} connection
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyper-derived+functor"} hyper-derived functor
            pushforward applied to the de Rham complex
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi R
                      %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi S
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}^q\pi_*(\Omega_{X/S}^\bullet)
          %p
            We will denote the relative Frobenius map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: X\to X^{(p)}
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{(p)}
            is the pullback of the structure map and the absolute Frobenius
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi ab
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{ab}: S\to S
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi π
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{(p)}=X\otimes_{\pi^{-1}(\mathcal{O}_S)} \pi^{-1}(\mathcal{O}_S)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}^\bullet
            is a complex of sheaves, then we denote by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}^q(\mathcal{A}^\bullet)
            the sheaf that is obtained by taking cohomology with respect to the maps of the complex.
          %h2#the_cartier_isomorphism The Cartier Isomorphism
          %p
            Suppose that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is an
            = succeed "-scheme" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/S
            is smooth, then there is a unique map of graded
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{X^{(p)}}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi S
                    %mi i
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ∼
                  %msup
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo *
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi S
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{-1}: \Omega^i_{X^{(p)}/S} \stackrel{\sim}{\to} \mathcal{H}^i(F_*\Omega^\bullet_{X/S})
            that satisfies:
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{-1}(1)=1
            ,
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{-1}(\omega\wedge \tau)=C^{-1}(\omega)\wedge C^{-1}(\tau)
          %p
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %msubsup
                    %mi F
                    %mi ab
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi d
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{-1}(d F_{ab}^{-1}(f))=[f^{p-1}d f]
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℋ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mo *
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi S
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}^1(F_*\Omega^\bullet_{X/S})
          %p The inverse of this isomorphism is the traditional Cartier isomorphism.
          %p
            The construction is quite simple. First note that we can immediately reduce to constructing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{-1}
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i=1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{-1}(1)=1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{-1}
            is
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{X^{(p)}}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i=0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{-1}
            is determined for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i=1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i\geq 1
            is determined from the second property.
          %p
            Now to construct for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i=1
            we just note that such a map is equivalent to a
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\pi^{(p)})^{-1}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℋ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mo *
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi S
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{X^{(p)}}\to \mathcal{H}^1(F_*\Omega_{X/S}^\bullet)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi S
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta: \mathcal{O}_X\times \pi^{-1}(\mathcal{O}_S)\to \mathcal{H}^1(\Omega_{X/S}^\bullet)
            that is biadditive and satisfies the extra three properties
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mi p
                  %mi s
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta(f s, s')=\delta(f, s^p s')
            ,
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mi p
                  %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mi p
                  %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta(g f, s)=g^p\delta(f,s)+f^p\delta(g,s)
            and
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi d
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta(f,1)=[f^{p-1}d f]
            \.
          %p
            Now define the map explicitly by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi s
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi d
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta(f,s)=[s f^{p-1}d f]
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{-1}
          %h2#relation_to_the_hodgede_rham_spectral_sequence Relation to the Hodge-de Rham Spectral Sequence
          %p
            For this discussion let’s assume that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/k
            is proper and smooth. Deligne and Illusie had an insight that the degeneration of the Hodge-de Rham spectral sequence (HdR SS) is closely related to the Cartier isomorphism. Recall that the HdR SS is formed by taking the spectral sequence associated to hypercohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi k
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi dR
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1^{p,q}=H^q(X, \Omega^p_{X/k})\Rightarrow H^{p+q}_{dR}(X/k)
          %p
            Now notice that if we form the complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                    %mi i
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigoplus_{i}\Omega^i_{X^{(p)}}[-i]
            which is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^i
            in degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d=0
            everywhere, then the left side of the inverse Cartier isomorphism is exactly
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℋ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                      %mi i
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}^i(\bigoplus_{i}\Omega^i_{X^{(p)}}[-i])
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}^i
            of the complex
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mo *
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi k
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_*\Omega_{X/k}^\bullet
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi D
                      %mi qCoh
                      %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{D}(X^{(p)}):=\mathbf{D}^b_{qCoh}(X^{(p)})
          %p
            We can ask whether or not there is some map in the derived category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                    %mi i
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo *
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi k
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi: \bigoplus_{i}\Omega^i_{X^{(p)}}[-i] \to F_*\Omega_{X/k}^\bullet
            with the property that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}^i(\phi)=C^{-1}
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo *
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                    %mi i
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}^n(X, \Omega_X^\bullet)=\mathbf{H}^n(X^{(p)}, F_*\Omega_X^\bullet)\simeq \bigoplus_{i} H^{n-i}(X^{(p)}, \Omega_X^i)
            \. Thus the dimensions of the
            = succeed "-vector" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1
            term match the dimensions at the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            term. Since everything is a
            = succeed "-vector" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %h2#the_generalization_to_noncommutative_algebra The Generalization to Non-commutative algebra
          %p
            See Kaledin Non-commutative Hodge-to-de Rham degeneration via the method of Deligne-Illusie
            %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0611623"} on the arxiv
          %h2#references References
          %p Nilpotent Connections and the Monodromy Theorem by Nicholas M. Katz
          %p
            Relevements modulo
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
